 @imp_ct  until it runs out of VRAM. 

Most people really dont care about RT and while DLSS is a fine argument, you are just saying that a used card one can buy for 50-100$ more is faster. Not to mention at that price 6800XT is again a better buy than the 3080 cause of VRAM alone, especially that this grade of cards is not made for 1080p but for 1440p-4k.

Does not matter which camp you are on, there is no denying that AMD is a better value proposition.

 @SweatyFeetGirl  AMD's rx7600 has a higher TDP, its got MUCH worse productivity performance, nvidia's shadowplay and other features are much better than AMD counterparts, etc. Now, had AMD charged $300 for a 10gb 160bit rx7600 which was as fast as a rx6700xt, they'd have killed the rtx 4060 and rtx 4060ti in one fell swoop. 

Then all AMD would need to do is disable a few cuda cores and release that as the rx7500xt at $230 (remember, amd's original rx7600 was gonna have just 28 CU's instead of the full 32 it has now). 

Of course, being the greedy scumbags they are, they decided to follow nvidia.

 @SweatyFeetGirl  No, shadowplay is quite good. 

People who buy the 4060 to do some light productivity or you know, its the only one in their budget. Heck, plenty of people use the 3060 for productivity cause it had enough performance and more than enough vram. 

You also forgot about efficiency. 115w vs 170w. Its quite a difference.

 @SoftExo  The thing is, for those $300 bucks you could easily get the 10GB 6700 which is much better than the 4060.
Also, saying it is featureless because it doesn't have frame generation (which imho is quite an useless feature) is just stupid. AMD has FSR (that on higher settings is as good as DLSS, I noticed with Jedi Survivor, as it doesn't have DLSS, so I was forced to use it and I like it a lot) and raytracing too, although for this class of GPUs is another useless feature.
The performance that you can ALWAYS use is what really matter, not features here and there of dubious utility and that only some games support.

 @jebusnazareth1869  Whats AMD's alternative to shadowplay on their mobile GPU's? Oh right. Nothing. Cause mobile dGPU's from AMD don't deserve amd relive. Gotta jump through hoops to get it. And shadowplay doesn't tax the GPU much while being half decent in its recording quality and reduces file sizes to a good extent. These are things AMD's relive cannot match. 

